      "problem": "$2(4p+2q)+5q=${{field-1}}\n$p\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$q$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we distribute the $2$ over each of the terms in parentheses.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(4p+2q)+5p & = \\\\ 2\\cdot 4p+2\\cdot 2q+5q & = \\\\ (8p)+(4q)+5q & = \\\\ 8p+4q+5q & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we collect like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8p+4q+5q & = \\\\ 8p+(4q+5q) & = \\\\ 8\\,p+9\\,q\\end{aligned}\n$$",
